@@@!atrep

@@/ lexigramma: the dictionary markup language - a fresh
@@/ dialektos (not a litogramma extension: an entry is a
@@/ record, not discourse) built on koine, the common dialect,
@@/ for inline formatting, quotations, lists, notes and
@@/ references. Coverage target: TEI Lex-0 equivalence - the
@@/ strict DARIAH profile of TEI ch. 9 - improved where
@@/ reproducing major dictionaries (LSJ, OED, the bilinguals)
@@/ demands it. Where Lex-0 still permits prose-shaped laxity,
@@/ lexigramma demands structure: kanonizo validates the sense
@@/ tree and the homograph numbering, and there is no
@@/ dictScrap.
@@/
@@/ Conventions:
@@/ - Entries are autonym: the headword is the onym, homographs
@@/   disambiguate by taxis (bank-1, bank-2), and
@@/   cross-references address entries by name through the
@@/   koine ref @>(headword) with a typing genos.
@@/ - Sense taxis is explicit and validated at every depth,
@@/   numeric; alphabetic display (2a) is the register's
@@/   rendering of depth two. Sense numbers are citable
@@/   identity (s.v. δίκη, sense 3).
@@/ - Presentation (bold headwords, label italics, column
@@/   layout) belongs entirely to exomorphoses.
@@/ - An abbreviations list is a koine definition list typed
@@/   .abbreviations after the title: each item's lemma the
@@/   abbreviation as the labels print it, its definition the
@@/   expansion. Labels in the text stay the abbreviation; the
@@/   list resolves them.
@@/ - Text shown only in a full reading (a secondary gloss, the
@@/   expanded translation) is an inline diaphane typed
@@/   .secondary; a short rendering may leave it out.
@@/ - Media attached to an entry (a pronunciation recording, an
@@/   illustration) is the core enmedia block inside the entry.

@@::koine

@=== entry
@![(taxis)] lemma
autonym
grammata
!@
@"dictionary entry; the lemma is the headword and registers as the onym, the taxis is the homograph number (per-lemma 1..n); nests for idioms, phrasal verbs and compounds (TEI Lex-0 entry/re)"@
===@

@=== sense
@:(taxis) [lemma]
grammata
:@
@"sense; explicit numeric taxis at every depth, validated; nested senses subdivide; the optional lemma is a gloss-title; definition text is the plain paragraphs within (TEI Lex-0 sense/def)"@
===@

@=== variant
@=~ grammata ~=@
@"variant form of the headword: alternate spelling, dialect form, inflected principal part; repeatable, genos-refinable (.spelling, .dialect, .inflection) (TEI Lex-0 form/orth)"@
===@

@=== pronunciation
@=% grammata %=@
@"pronunciation; repeatable, genos-typed by system (.ipa, .respell) (TEI Lex-0 form/pron)"@
===@

@=== syllabification
@=- grammata -=@
@"syllabified or hyphenated headword (TEI Lex-0 form/hyph)"@
===@

@=== grammar
@=& grammata &=@
@"the entry's grammatical line: part of speech, gender, inflectional class; genos-refinable (.pos, .gen, .num) (TEI Lex-0 gramGrp)"@
===@

@=== grammar-label
@& grammata &@
@"inline grammatical label within a sense or form line (pl., fem., intr.); genos-refinable like the grammar line (TEI Lex-0 gram)"@
===@

@=== etymology
@=< grammata >=@
@"etymology: the derivation chain, language names carried as usage labels with .lang (TEI Lex-0 etym)"@
===@

@=== usage-label
@[ grammata ]@
@"usage label, in the brackets dictionaries print them in; genos-typed: .reg register, .dom domain, .geo geography, .time period, .lang language (TEI Lex-0 usg)"@
===@

@=== equivalent
@=> grammata <=@
@"translation equivalent in a bilingual entry; the target language rides a genos (.fr, .de, .grc) (TEI Lex-0 cit[@type=translationEquivalent])"@
===@

@=== citation
@~ grammata ~@
@"inline citation: the quoted illustrative text; the source follows as a koine ref into the source registry, the locus and date as plain text (TEI Lex-0 cit/quote)"@
===@

@=== citation-block
@=~~
grammata
~~=@
@"citation paragraph, the OED shape: date, author, work, locus, quotation as one dated block; repeatable within a sense"@
===@

@=== inflection
@=* grammata *=@
@"inflected form of the headword, registered as a lookup key and nothing more: print registers do not display it, the Kindle exomorphosis compiles it into the lookup index; repeatable, typically embedded from a sourced inflection dataset at authoring time (e.g. tools/inflect-ru.py from OpenRussian); typed .sort it is the key the headword is sorted and found under when that differs from the headword as displayed (a headword whose displayed part is not indexed: DSL's braces) (TEI Lex-0 form[type=inflected])"@
===@

@=== languages
@=/ grammata /=@
@"the dictionary's languages as language codes, the index (headword) language first, then the contents language; one line after the title; a monolingual dictionary names one"@
===@
